# Compare two reasoning methods

## Section

One Agent has two DSL profiles and two routes. The mock responses use each
method's expected text format. This compares result routing, not reasoning
quality. Change `backend` to `:live` to explore both with `OPENAI_API_KEY`.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:text, "Step 1: Add 2 and 3.\nConclusion: 5"}},
  %{reply: {:text, "1. Add the values.\n#### 5"}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)

context =
  if mock do
    options = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)
    %{ai: %{cot: %{options: options}, cod: %{options: options}}}
  else
    %{}
  end
```

## Define two profiles

```elixir
defmodule Guide.ReasoningMethods do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_reasoning_methods"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{reply: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.default("")})

    ai :cot do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      reasoning :chain_of_thought

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
      end

      result into: :reply
    end

    ai :cod do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      reasoning :chain_of_draft

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
      end

      result into: :reply
    end
  end

  routes do
    route "guides.ai.cot", ai: :cot
    route "guides.ai.cod", ai: :cod
  end
end
```

## Run both profiles

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.ReasoningMethods, id: "guide-reasoning-methods")

{:ok, cot} = Guide.ReasoningMethods.ask_sync(server, "What is 2 + 3?", profile: :cot, context: context)
{:ok, cod} = Guide.ReasoningMethods.ask_sync(server, "What is 2 + 3?", profile: :cod, context: context)

%{chain_of_thought: cot, chain_of_draft: cod}
```

Both mock conclusions are `"5"`. The internal steps and raw responses have
method-specific accessors. The two profiles share one AgentServer but retain
separate method results.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [_, _]} = Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)
end

:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Choose a reasoning method](../v3/08_reasoning_methods.md).
